1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kisskh.asia =

2
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:14,800
[Connecting to You]

3
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,010
It was the landlord.

4
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:20,620
He said the renovation was going smoothly.

5
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,860
I should be able to move back
the week after next.

6
00:01:29,539 --> 00:01:30,800
Why move?

7
00:01:35,410 --> 00:01:37,120
I thought you were afraid that

8
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:40,000
people at the station
would know we live together.

9
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,979
That was true at first.

10
00:01:47,539 --> 00:01:49,080
Then that's it.

11
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:13,870
[The 10th Thread]

12
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:21,140
[Self-fulfilling Prophecy]
[Things Happen as You Expect]

13
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:25,120
Come on, make some room.

14
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,640
Chicken, fish.

15
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,290
Neither of you is allowed to eat,

16
00:02:32,290 --> 00:02:33,730
because you two ran away together.

17
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:35,550
Runaways get no chicken or fish.

18
00:02:35,579 --> 00:02:36,579
They're all mine.

19
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:37,930
Chaonan,

20
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,250
don't be so childish.

21
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:41,500
-You guys should eat together.
-Yeah, don't be so childish.

22
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:43,000
-So childish.
-Grandma.

23
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,450
Alright, since you're back,
let me feed you a shrimp, okay?

24
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:47,829
Here, eat more shrimp.

25
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:50,079
-Are there any egg dumplings left?
-Grandma.

26
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:51,079
Grandma, have some shrimp too.

27
00:02:51,079 --> 00:02:52,040
Okay, thanks.

28
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:54,120
Put some more egg dumplings in for me.

29
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:56,530
Let me answer the phone.

30
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:01,370
Hello, Juan.

31
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:03,760
What's up?

32
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:05,620
Play cards?

33
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:06,620
No.

34
00:03:07,070 --> 00:03:09,130
Not tonight. You go play.

35
00:03:09,170 --> 00:03:10,790
My grandson is back.

36
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,480
Jiakai.

37
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,140
Did you forget?

38
00:03:17,290 --> 00:03:18,770
What's wrong with Jiakai?

39
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:24,370
Grandma, come eat.

40
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:25,570
It's getting cold.

41
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:28,120
Jiakai,

42
00:03:28,290 --> 00:03:29,660
did you go

43
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:32,190
apply for a job
at Nanxiong Plastics Factory?

44
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:36,020
Looks like you did.

45
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:39,450
When Juan asked me,

46
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:41,610
I didn't believe it.

47
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:01,540
I think I finished

48
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:03,250
all the drinks in the fridge.

49
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:06,660
You two go to the convenience store
and buy some for me.

50
00:04:21,790 --> 00:04:24,270
You were doing so well
studying psychology.

51
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:28,090
Why do you want to work
at a plastics factory?

52
00:04:33,870 --> 00:04:35,930
The pay at Nanxiong is good,

53
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,190
and it's a stable job.

54
00:04:37,370 --> 00:04:38,940
It's also quite close to home.

55
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:41,140
I can get there in 30 minutes by scooter.

56
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,800
You can find a better job there

57
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,420
or go to grad school.

58
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:50,110
Why come back to the countryside?

59
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:53,000
The jobs there aren't necessarily
better than here.

60
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,409
And I applied for
the development department.

61
00:04:55,409 --> 00:04:57,290
It's an office job too.

62
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:59,659
I can also live at home
and keep you company.

63
00:04:59,659 --> 00:05:02,600
Don't keep me company, please.

64
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:06,370
Why don't you want me
to come back and keep you company?

65
00:05:08,270 --> 00:05:10,460
If you dare to work at that factory,

66
00:05:10,490 --> 00:05:11,690
I'll kick you out.

67
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,050
How can you do that?

68
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:14,930
Grandma, this is emotional blackmail.

69
00:05:14,930 --> 00:05:17,020
I don't care what emotional blackmail is.

70
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:19,080
You're just not allowed to move back.

71
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:30,410
-Jiakai!
-Jiakai!

72
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:35,530
Jiakai!

73
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:36,480
Jiakai!

74
00:05:36,909 --> 00:05:39,040
Dad, Mom.

75
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:41,320
Jiakai!

76
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,340
-Jiakai!
-Jiakai!

77
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:42,780
Here!

78
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,750
Come here quickly.

79
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:45,620
Didn't you want to ride the Ferris wheel?

80
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:47,159
Let's go line up.

81
00:05:50,409 --> 00:05:51,620
I don't want to.

82
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:52,750
Why?

83
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:55,750
Haven't you been looking forward to it
for a long time?

84
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:57,990
I don't understand.

85
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,340
Why can you just get up and leave,

86
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:02,490
tossing me aside like that?

87
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:07,870
Jiakai, I'm sorry.

88
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,610
We really love you.

89
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:12,110
I know.

90
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:17,650
I know.

91
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,670
Jiakai!

92
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,570
Jiakai!

93
00:06:20,830 --> 00:06:22,370
Jiakai, come here quickly.

94
00:06:22,790 --> 00:06:23,650
-Jiakai!
-Jiakai!

95
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:24,370
Jiakai!

96
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:24,960
Jiakai!

97
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:25,860
Come here quickly.

98
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,110
Jiakai!

99
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:30,410
We really want to continue
watching you grow up.

100
00:06:30,410 --> 00:06:32,650
Then figure out a way to stay.

101
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:43,900
You're awake.

102
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,390
Are you okay?

103
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:47,870
My head hurts so much.

104
00:06:50,790 --> 00:06:52,500
How did I get back yesterday?

105
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:56,310
Chaonan and I went out to look for you.

106
00:06:56,530 --> 00:06:58,750
We found you passed out drunk in the park,

107
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:00,010
so we carried you back.

108
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,880
How did you manage to get so drunk?

109
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:07,710
How bad was the fight
with your grandmother?

110
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:13,130
I don't know how to explain it.

111
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:15,150
I'm going to be late.

112
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,120
No, no, no.

113
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:20,580
I don't have to work today.

114
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,790
Why is it gone?

115
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:25,690
What's gone?

116
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:31,410
Sweating a little.

117
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:35,220
No.

118
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:37,050
I can't see the threads anymore.

119
00:07:37,050 --> 00:07:38,640
Then look more carefully.

120
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:42,240
I think your eye boogers
are blocking your view.

121
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,460
Don't you think?

122
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:47,620
No. They're not in any of the photos.

123
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:54,060
How could this happen?

124
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,580
Did I drink too much yesterday?

125
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:59,320
Or did I do something after getting drunk?

126
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:02,760
This is a bit troublesome.

127
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:03,680
After the long holiday,

128
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:06,080
the Psychic Club is fully booked,
you know?

129
00:08:06,250 --> 00:08:07,510
What should we do then?

130
00:08:08,370 --> 00:08:09,370
Nothing we can do.

131
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:11,500
Jiakai, Chaonan.

132
00:08:11,790 --> 00:08:14,050
I've already put your luggage in the car.

133
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:16,330
We can leave later when you're ready.

134
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,620
-Got it.
-Got it.

135
00:08:20,410 --> 00:08:22,490
Alright, how about this?

136
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:23,980
You go back first,

137
00:08:24,870 --> 00:08:27,600
and we'll figure out
the thread situation later.

138
00:08:27,770 --> 00:08:30,900
I think you'll be fine
after resting for a couple of days.

139
00:08:31,670 --> 00:08:32,400
Fine.

140
00:08:32,789 --> 00:08:34,600
Let's go. Give me your phone.

141
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:39,630
Grandma!

142
00:08:39,659 --> 00:08:41,789
Your favorite Chaonan is leaving!

143
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:44,450
Jiakai and Dawei are leaving too!

144
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:46,720
If you don't come out and say goodbye,

145
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,910
we'll never see each other again!

146
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,350
I know!

147
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:52,860
Goodbye, goodbye!

148
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:54,320
So noisy!

149
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:57,450
Forget it. Grandma is always like this
when she's angry.

150
00:08:57,450 --> 00:08:58,980
Let her be alone for a while.

151
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,170
Grandma.

152
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,350
We're leaving.

153
00:09:21,270 --> 00:09:25,850
[Temporarily closed...
until further notice]

154
00:09:25,850 --> 00:09:29,140
[Psychic Club] [General Classroom]

155
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:32,760
[Psychic Club] [General Classroom]

156
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:41,220
[Due to personal reasons,
the Psychic Club is temporarily closed.]

157
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:41,920
[Until further notice.]

158
00:09:41,950 --> 00:09:43,910
[Closing the club suddenly sucks.]

159
00:09:43,910 --> 00:09:45,060
[Did something happen?]
[No integrity at all.]

160
00:09:44,370 --> 00:09:46,110
Are netizens only leaving comments here,

161
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:45,940
[It sucks.] [Scammers.]

162
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:48,260
or is it the same on other social media?

163
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:51,620
It's the same on other social media.

164
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:54,840
Sorry.

165
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:58,340
It's all because my powers
suddenly disappeared.

166
00:09:58,360 --> 00:09:59,890
Idiot.

167
00:10:00,290 --> 00:10:01,690
Why are you apologizing?

168
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:06,100
Didn't you always say
you wanted to be a normal person?

169
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:06,770
Look.

170
00:10:07,510 --> 00:10:09,000
Now your wish has come true.

171
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,040
Look at you now.

172
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,250
How normal you are.

173
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:14,750
Shouldn't you be happy?

174
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:16,630
Am I normal now?

175
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:20,520
My mom said when you do chores,

176
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:21,950
you can forget your troubles.

177
00:10:21,950 --> 00:10:24,410
So mopping the floor
is the right thing to do.

178
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:26,390
Mop it.

179
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:55,360
[Dawei] [Need help moving?]

180
00:10:55,390 --> 00:10:58,080
[It's okay. I've already moved.]

181
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:09,280
[Starlight Gala]

182
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:09,820
There will be a lucky draw
and dance-partner matching later.

183
00:11:12,950 --> 00:11:14,240
The number tag.

184
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:16,620
Lin Jiakai, Lin Jiakai, Lin Jiakai.

185
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,370
Can you come in for a second?

186
00:11:18,370 --> 00:11:20,910
A junior who was just chatting
with me is super cute.

187
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:22,250
I think he's interested in me.

188
00:11:22,250 --> 00:11:24,250
Come in and help me check his thread.

189
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:25,910
I am now...

190
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:28,110
I forgot you can't see it for now. Sorry.

191
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,290
It's fine.

192
00:11:30,290 --> 00:11:31,890
Then after you finish
handing out the number tags,

193
00:11:31,890 --> 00:11:33,250
hurry in and join the fun.

194
00:11:33,250 --> 00:11:34,990
I'll handle the junior myself.

195
00:11:44,250 --> 00:11:46,160
Didn't we agree to have dinner together?

196
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,490
What are you doing here?

197
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:51,050
I didn't realize so much time had passed.

198
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:54,860
Sorry. Why didn't you call me?

199
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,160
I did.

200
00:11:57,410 --> 00:11:58,660
I also texted you.

201
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
You didn't answer or reply, did you?

202
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:07,410
Sorry, I turned off my phone alerts.

203
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,810
How did you find me?

204
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:14,750
I figured there were only
a few places you'd go,

205
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:17,160
and that I should be able to find you.

206
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,160
What were you doing?

207
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,150
I was just wandering around

208
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,400
and found this water gun someone forgot.

209
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:31,750
Let me see.

210
00:12:40,170 --> 00:12:41,160
What's wrong?

211
00:12:41,910 --> 00:12:44,790
Did you help someone
and get into trouble again?

212
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:46,570
No, I didn't.

213
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:50,040
Just tell the truth.

214
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:52,750
I'll hold back
from scolding you this time.

215
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,160
I really didn't.

216
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:58,680
Are you going to confess honestly?

217
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:10,380
I just...

218
00:13:12,410 --> 00:13:13,500
can't see threads.

219
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,100
Can't see threads?

220
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:18,870
What do you mean?

221
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:22,160
Ever since I came back
from Grandma's house,

222
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:24,000
I haven't been able to see any threads.

223
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,170
Why didn't you tell me

224
00:13:25,170 --> 00:13:26,720
such an important thing earlier?

225
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:29,470
You don't tell me
every important thing either.

226
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,660
You seem to care about me a lot,

227
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:38,790
starting treating me as a real friend.

228
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:41,740
But actually, you don't tell me
important things.

229
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,270
You haven't told me
about your family either.

230
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,130
To be blunt,

231
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:48,120
you don't trust me at all.

232
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:50,250
Now that I've moved out of your place,

233
00:13:50,250 --> 00:13:52,050
you must feel much more relaxed.

234
00:13:57,750 --> 00:14:00,210
I really didn't expect you
to see me this way.

235
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:02,430
Isn't that what you think?

236
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:06,620
Because you never told me
your true thoughts either.

237
00:14:08,630 --> 00:14:10,520
Why are we talking so much here?

238
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:12,950
We don't understand each other anyway.

239
00:14:15,370 --> 00:14:16,410
Where are you going?

240
00:14:16,410 --> 00:14:17,620
Going home.

241
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,930
We haven't even made things clear.

242
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,290
My phone is ringing.

243
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:35,120
Hello?

244
00:14:35,530 --> 00:14:36,530
Uncle Liao.

245
00:14:43,310 --> 00:14:44,310
What's wrong?

246
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:49,280
My grandma is in the hospital.

247
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:57,750
Go up and stay with your grandmother.

248
00:14:57,750 --> 00:14:59,870
I'll go up in a bit. Be safe.

249
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:00,750
Okay.

250
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:07,350
Go ahead.

251
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:08,430
Okay.

252
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:29,730
Grandma.

253
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:35,070
How did you know?

254
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:38,250
Uncle Liao called me.

255
00:15:38,250 --> 00:15:39,860
He said you fell
and were sent to the hospital.

256
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:40,960
So I came back.

257
00:15:41,210 --> 00:15:43,210
How did you hurt yourself like this?

258
00:15:45,550 --> 00:15:49,970
That Liao. I told him not to make a fuss.

259
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:51,970
I'm fine.

260
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:53,390
I just...

261
00:15:53,750 --> 00:15:56,540
fell down the stairs, and that's all.

262
00:15:57,410 --> 00:16:00,000
I'll stay and take care of you
for the next few days.

263
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,250
No need. Why would you stay?

264
00:16:02,250 --> 00:16:03,750
Don't you have classes?

265
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:07,870
The doctor said my legs are fine.

266
00:16:07,870 --> 00:16:11,690
I just need to be observed
for a concussion.

267
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:13,500
If there isn't one, I can go home.

268
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:15,020
So you should hurry back.

269
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:18,410
Even if you go home, you still need
someone to take care of you.

270
00:16:18,410 --> 00:16:19,500
No need. Not at all.

271
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:22,510
I can take good care of myself.

272
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:25,880
Go back. Hurry up and go back.

273
00:16:26,130 --> 00:16:27,190
Otherwise,

274
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:29,820
there won't be any buses left
for you to go back.

275
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:33,010
Do you really want me
to go back that much?

276
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,670
Hurry up and leave.

277
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:39,450
Okay, whatever you say.

278
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:52,910
Grandma.

279
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:56,370
Why are you back again?

280
00:16:57,290 --> 00:16:59,070
I forgot my backpack.

281
00:17:04,869 --> 00:17:06,130
I'm sorry.

282
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,619
Why are you sorry?

283
00:17:12,790 --> 00:17:15,619
It's not like you made me fall.

284
00:17:15,619 --> 00:17:17,810
Why are you sorry?

285
00:17:17,829 --> 00:17:20,450
I shouldn't have argued
with you like that.

286
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:23,510
No need to apologize.

287
00:17:28,950 --> 00:17:30,950
You were right.

288
00:17:30,950 --> 00:17:35,700
I shouldn't have kept scolding
your parents like that before.

289
00:17:37,870 --> 00:17:41,160
The one to blame the most is myself.

290
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:43,660
Grandma, don't be like this.

291
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:45,390
I didn't mean that.

292
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,410
Your family of three was going on a trip.

293
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:54,250
It was rescheduled, right?

294
00:17:55,750 --> 00:17:57,150
What was wrong with that?

295
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:01,220
It was all because of me.

296
00:18:02,870 --> 00:18:05,000
I sprained my back.

297
00:18:05,870 --> 00:18:08,620
Your mom stayed to take care of me,

298
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:10,410
so it was delayed.

299
00:18:11,910 --> 00:18:15,280
That's why the car accident happened.

300
00:18:20,130 --> 00:18:22,610
I often think,

301
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:26,790
if your mom hadn't taken care of me,

302
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:31,750
that wouldn't have happened.

303
00:18:33,290 --> 00:18:35,160
That's why I said

304
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:38,120
I didn't want you to take care of me.

305
00:18:38,260 --> 00:18:41,050
Wherever you want to build your career,

306
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:42,750
just go there.

307
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:46,290
Don't worry about me.

308
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:50,750
I really don't want to be your burden.

309
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:52,750
I know, Grandma.

310
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:56,980
But...

311
00:18:57,370 --> 00:18:58,970
if you ever want to come back,

312
00:18:59,250 --> 00:19:01,160
I'll always be waiting for you.

313
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:04,120
Are you not kicking me out?

314
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:06,290
Why would I kick you out?

315
00:19:06,290 --> 00:19:08,500
You are my grandson.

316
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,400
Where would I kick you to?

317
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:15,750
You need to think carefully for yourself.

318
00:19:15,750 --> 00:19:17,910
Do you understand what I'm saying?

319
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:19,650
I understand, Grandma.

320
00:19:19,870 --> 00:19:21,670
I will think about it carefully.

321
00:19:21,690 --> 00:19:23,900
Love you.

322
00:19:27,410 --> 00:19:29,290
Careful, Grandma.

323
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:31,250
Careful, careful.

324
00:19:31,490 --> 00:19:32,510
Sit here.

325
00:19:32,530 --> 00:19:33,660
Okay, okay.

326
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,900
It's still more comfortable at home.

327
00:19:49,050 --> 00:19:51,400
Much better than a hospital bed.

328
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:53,410
Grandma, you rest well.

329
00:19:55,040 --> 00:19:56,540
I'll go park the car.

330
00:19:57,870 --> 00:20:00,120
Turn right after you
drive out of the alley.

331
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,970
There are more parking spaces there.

332
00:20:01,970 --> 00:20:02,790
Okay.

333
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:14,700
He really is a nice young man.

334
00:20:14,730 --> 00:20:16,360
He works hard

335
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:19,290
and is polite.

336
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,160
Yeah.

337
00:20:24,070 --> 00:20:24,760
Yeah?

338
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:28,660
Do you like him?

339
00:20:54,990 --> 00:20:55,610
[Peggy Talks Love Psychology]

340
00:20:55,410 --> 00:20:56,650
Two-Minute Love Live Stream.

341
00:20:55,610 --> 00:20:56,570
[Two-Minute Love Live Stream]

342
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,880
It's fleeting, so don't miss it.

343
00:20:59,060 --> 00:20:59,800
Hello, everyone.

344
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:00,410
Sorry.

345
00:21:00,410 --> 00:21:01,120
Today,

346
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:02,430
I had a little argument

347
00:21:02,450 --> 00:21:03,250
with my husband.

348
00:21:03,250 --> 00:21:04,590
So if I lose my temper

349
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:05,920
later,

350
00:21:05,950 --> 00:21:07,700
please forgive me, okay?

351
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,510
I will still maintain my professionalism

352
00:21:09,510 --> 00:21:10,450
and share with you something.

353
00:21:10,450 --> 00:21:11,510
What I want to share today

354
00:21:11,510 --> 00:21:13,160
is a psychological theory.

355
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,050
What I'm going to talk about today

356
00:21:14,050 --> 00:21:14,540
is

357
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:16,280
the self-fulfilling prophecy.

358
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:18,360
Self-fulfilling prophecy.

359
00:21:18,450 --> 00:21:19,700
For example,

360
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,490
you often hear that a bank

361
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:22,160
might be

362
00:21:22,190 --> 00:21:23,250
in danger of going bankrupt,

363
00:21:23,250 --> 00:21:24,950
causing a bank run,

364
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,870
and it actually goes bankrupt.

365
00:21:26,870 --> 00:21:27,890
Or,

366
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:28,320
a guy

367
00:21:28,340 --> 00:21:29,830
thinks his girlfriend is surrounded

368
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,120
by many handsome guys,

369
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:32,200
say, handsome colleagues.

370
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:33,450
He starts to worry

371
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,830
and feels insecure every day,

372
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:35,390
thinking that

373
00:21:35,390 --> 00:21:37,480
his girlfriend will cheat on him one day.

374
00:21:35,490 --> 00:21:37,310
[Would you ever cheat on someone someday?]

375
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,540
As a result, he annoys the girl,

376
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:41,620
and she actually breaks up with him.

377
00:21:41,670 --> 00:21:43,420
To me,

378
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:45,870
I personally hate those

379
00:21:45,870 --> 00:21:47,830
who like to check their horoscopes
every day

380
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,730
[Seems to imply something]

381
00:21:47,830 --> 00:21:48,640
and then align themselves

382
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,250
